[{"id":2892380279,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6sZjh3","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","login":"dsnopek","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek"},"body":"I think making `Object::has_method()` virtual should be discussed with the core team\r\n\r\nPersonally, I have kind of mixed feelings about it. This will mean that there are methods that will return `true` for `has_method()` but that won't be included in `get_method_list()`, which isn't currently the case.\r\n\r\nWe already have `JavaClass::get_java_method_list()` to list methods from Java - perhaps we should just add a `JavaClass::has_java_method()` and not mess with `Object`?","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-2892380279","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-06-03T13:34:58Z"},{"id":2892937767,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6sbron","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","login":"dsnopek","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-2892937767","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2025-06-03T15:06:29Z"},{"id":2896644130,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6sp0gi","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"I'm not sure this is a great idea.\r\n\r\nThis would introduce a path for `Object` subclasses to define methods that are not registered in `ClassDB`, introducing 'dynamic typing' as a whole new concept to our ecosystem. Adding this would make it impossible (or at least much harder) to cache method pointers on a `Class` level, which is something I've shown in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/106646 to accelerate property access by at least 60% (with potential for more).\r\n\r\nIs there some other way this could be resolved? Perhaps this is just an indication for Java functions to register their existing methods in `ClassDB` (or in the scripts way)?","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-2896644130","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-06-04T13:02:03Z"},{"id":3126214047,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc66Vj2f","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?u=25817fe797fcc7a812ba9d7f58f593f5a003abbb&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","login":"syntaxerror247","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-3126214047","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-08-17T06:54:01Z"},{"id":3126216686,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc66Vkfu","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?u=25817fe797fcc7a812ba9d7f58f593f5a003abbb&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","login":"syntaxerror247","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-3126216686","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/107075","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-08-17T07:05:35Z"},{"id":3126217154,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc66VknC","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/176927541?u=25817fe797fcc7a812ba9d7f58f593f5a003abbb&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/syntaxerror247","id":176927541,"node_id":"U_kgDOCouzNQ","login":"syntaxerror247","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/syntaxerror247"},"body":"I skimmed through the changes; looks good to me!","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/107075#pullrequestreview-3126217154","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repo